<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The control bar's one subtitle control.

    REPLACES FIVE VIEWS: a CC icon, two nudge arrows, an offset read-out and a
    reset. Those timing controls live behind this button now, because timing is
    adjusted rarely and judged by watching, while the bar is navigated constantly
    on a d-pad.

    IT WEARS THE BAND'S OWN BACKGROUND. It used to carry a hairline white outline
    at 3dp radius, from a time when it sat among media3's bare glyphs and had to
    announce itself as something pressable. Every control beside it is now a
    10dp rounded fill with a blue focus ring, so the outline was the only thing
    in the row still speaking the old language. Sharing player_pill_bg means it
    also shares the focus treatment, which is the part that has to match.

    ICON AND TEXT, not either alone. The glyph is what the eye finds in the
    row; the words are what make the state readable without decoding opacity,
    which is what an icon on its own asked of you at three metres.

    MEDIUM, not regular. It is the only text in the band that is a control
    rather than a read-out, and at 14sp on a panel several metres away regular
    Roboto thins out next to the solid glyphs beside it. Bold was too loud for
    a label that is read once; medium just stops it looking skinny.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="40dp"
    android:layout_gravity="center_vertical"
    android:paddingStart="16dp"
    android:paddingEnd="16dp"
    android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
    android:textColor="#FFDBE4F6"
    android:textSize="14sp"
    android:fontFamily="sans-serif-medium"
    android:includeFontPadding="false"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:drawableStart="@drawable/ic_player_cc"
    android:drawablePadding="9dp"
    android:maxLines="1"
    android:ellipsize="end"
    android:maxWidth="260dp"
    android:focusable="true"
    android:clickable="true"
    android:text="Subtitles" />
